Use this structure:

```txt
prisma/
  schema.prisma
  seed.ts
src/
  main.ts
  app.module.ts
  common/
  config/
  prisma/
  modules/
```

# NestJS Modules

Each domain lives in `src/modules/<domain>/`.

Standard structure:

- `<domain>.module.ts`
- `<domain>.controller.ts`
- `<domain>.service.ts`
- `dto/create-<domain>.dto.ts`
- `dto/update-<domain>.dto.ts`

Controllers handle HTTP only.
Services contain business logic.
DTO classes validate request input.
Use NestJS exceptions instead of manual error objects.
